   "notes": "The head was trained on bone-marrow CITE-seq (NeurIPS 2021); on melanoma cells it is out of its training distribution. Declared choice: use it as trained (head stages then test this head on new cells). Cells are labelled from their detected guides, not from the file's perturbation column (which calls 13,316 IFN-gamma cells \"control\" although they have no guide or guides for other genes): a control cell has only non-targeting guides, a treated cell only guides for one target gene (plus any non-targeting guides); cells with no guide or with guides for two genes are left out. Genes reach TEDDY through the 10x GRCh38-3.0.0 symbol table that teddy_mm uses (tools/gene_map.py): the file's own Ensembl ids put HLA-A, -B, -C, -E, B2M and IFNGR2 on alternate-haplotype ids outside TEDDY's vocabulary, which would drop exactly the MHC genes before TEDDY.\n"
